WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:12.740
Renewing a passport. Signing up for Medicare. Each one can mean a different agency, a different website, a different form.

2
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.140
The White House says Americans spend around 10 billion hours a year on federal paperwork.

3
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:25.380
America.gov, launched on September 29, is meant to be one front door.

4
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:33.840
You ask a question in plain language. It looks for the answer across about 29.000 official government websites.

5
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.760
According to the team behind it, it runs on SI models from Google and xAI.

6
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:46.080
Some services stay out entirely, like IRS tax filing and national security systems.

7
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:53.200
For now, it's mainly an information service. The head of the GSA said people need to start with something simple.

8
00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:02.100
The site says its SI providers don't keep your questions. The test ahead: accurate answers, and privacy that holds up.
